1
00:00:05,571 --> 00:00:08,969
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۞

2
00:00:09,477 --> 00:00:11,157
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۞

3
00:00:13,094 --> 00:00:17,746
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

4
00:00:18,254 --> 00:00:24,253
Continuing with the response of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) towards the message of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

5
00:00:24,764 --> 00:00:28,765
We talked about a few yesterday, we'll continue with the rest.

6
00:00:29,153 --> 00:00:30,354
Number eight,

7
00:00:31,064 --> 00:00:35,616
they would try to put Muhammadﷺ under pressure.

8
00:00:36,967 --> 00:00:43,511
They were persistent, they would never give up, they would keep on trying every method

9
00:00:44,914 --> 00:00:51,424
including, using his close uncle Abu Talib(ابوطالب) to pressure him.

10
00:00:52,768 --> 00:00:54,959
In this narration, we have over here,

11
00:00:55,395 --> 00:00:59,990
Aqeel(عقيل), the son of Abu Talib(ابوطالب), he narrates and says that

12
00:01:00,483 --> 00:01:05,078
the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they came to Abu Talib(ابوطالب), and they told him;

13
00:01:05,118 --> 00:01:11,001
This nephew of yours is disrupting and disturbing us in our meetings and in our mosque.

14
00:01:11,866 --> 00:01:15,222
So, they consider the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ to be disruption.

15
00:01:16,665 --> 00:01:19,040
So, tell him to stay away from us.

16
00:01:20,404 --> 00:01:23,301
 Abu Talib(ابوطالب) told Aqeel(عقيل), go and call Muhammad(محمد) for me.

17
00:01:25,390 --> 00:01:27,330
So, Aqeel(عقيل) said: I found him in Qanas(قَنَسْ),

18
00:01:27,464 --> 00:01:30,226
Qanas(قَنَسْ) means, a very small room or a tent

19
00:01:30,338 --> 00:01:32,926
and it was noon time very hot in Makkah.

20
00:01:33,339 --> 00:01:37,541
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ came to meet his uncle Abu Talib(ابوطالب).

21
00:01:39,206 --> 00:01:42,130
So, his uncle Abu Talib(ابوطالب) told him, that your people are complaining

22
00:01:42,553 --> 00:01:46,564
and saying that you are disrupting them, and you are disturbing them in their meetings.

23
00:01:47,125 --> 00:01:48,446
So, why don't you stop.

24
00:01:50,096 --> 00:01:57,128
And Abu Talib(ابوطالب) was not speaking to Muhammadﷺ, in a tone of an order, do this!

25
00:01:57,453 --> 00:02:04,571
But he was telling him as an advice, it's better, you know, so that you would not (harm or) have your people upset,

26
00:02:04,981 --> 00:02:12,511
how about if you stop disturbing them or disrupting their meetings, in a very kind way.

27
00:02:13,223 --> 00:02:15,905
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Talib(ابوطالب)

28
00:02:16,691 --> 00:02:20,612
Rasool Ullah, he looked at the sky and he pointed it to the sun and told Abu Talib(ابوطالب),

29
00:02:20,692 --> 00:02:22,293
O my uncle, Do you see the sun?

30
00:02:22,782 --> 00:02:23,743
He said: Yes.

31
00:02:24,550 --> 00:02:33,059
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I am no more capable of stopping that, than you are, of getting me a flame from it.

32
00:02:35,752 --> 00:02:38,381
In other words, it's impossible for me to stop this.

33
00:02:38,929 --> 00:02:42,623
Just like it is impossible for you to get a flame from this sun.

34
00:02:43,837 --> 00:02:49,921
This is part of me, Da'wah(دعوة) is my life, spreading Islam is my mission,

35
00:02:50,228 --> 00:02:52,926
 I cannot give it up, it's impossible.

36
00:02:54,526 --> 00:02:57,620
And you must have heard of the narration when Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

37
00:02:57,982 --> 00:03:02,350
If they put the sun, on my right hand and the moon and my left hand

38
00:03:02,658 --> 00:03:10,430
I would not give up this matter, until Allah سبحانه وتعالى judges or I lose my life.

39
00:03:11,299 --> 00:03:12,844
That is a weaker narration.

40
00:03:13,312 --> 00:03:16,045
But we find the same meaning in the strong narration.

41
00:03:17,001 --> 00:03:19,476
That no matter what I will continue with this mission.

42
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:26,182
His uncle told him, O my nephew, you are telling the truth, I believe you, go ahead and continue.

43
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:30,485
So, Abu Talib(ابوطالب) was telling Muhammadﷺ, I believe you that you cannot give this up.

44
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:34,213
Go ahead, I will support you, do what Allah has told you to do.

45
00:03:35,685 --> 00:03:41,746
We see from this, that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are using every method, to try to sway Muhammadﷺ

46
00:03:42,137 --> 00:03:48,222
and they would never give up, I mean, even when Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Sahabah(صحابه), and we gonna talk about next.

47
00:03:49,184 --> 00:03:55,016
When the Messenger of Allah told the Sahabah(صحابه) to go to Al-Habasha(ألحبشه), to Abyssinia, so that they could flee from the persecution,

48
00:03:56,410 --> 00:04:06,426
still Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) weren't satisfied with that and they sent a delegation to ask An-Najashi(أنجاشي) to turn the Muslims over,

49
00:04:07,102 --> 00:04:07,832
Why.?

50
00:04:07,991 --> 00:04:11,919
Were the Muslims in Abyssinia any threat to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) politically?

51
00:04:11,959 --> 00:04:12,767
No.

52
00:04:13,150 --> 00:04:15,166
Were they, a threat economically? No.

53
00:04:15,824 --> 00:04:21,534
So, what is the reason Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are so persistent in following the Muslims even though the Muslims left them alone.

54
00:04:22,341 --> 00:04:25,745
So, the issue here, even if Rasool Allah ﷺ would have stopped,

55
00:04:26,472 --> 00:04:28,833
they wouldn't have left Rasool Allah ﷺ alone.

56
00:04:29,341 --> 00:04:34,653
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) wanted to stop this message, by all means possible.

57
00:04:35,879 --> 00:04:38,578
And if you would leave them alone, they won't leave you alone.

58
00:04:40,338 --> 00:04:42,653
Number nine:  Jealousy and hatred,

59
00:04:43,359 --> 00:04:46,361
Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره), one of the elders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), he said;

60
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:50,486
If Allah wanted to choose a Prophet, how come he didn't choose me?

61
00:04:51,647 --> 00:04:56,922
I'm more wealthy and wise and older than Muhammadﷺ,

62
00:04:57,930 --> 00:05:01,610
and there was a similar claim made by a man in At-Taef(ألطائف),

63
00:05:02,988 --> 00:05:06,898
now the two prominent towns of Hijaaz(حجاز) were Makkah and At-At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف).

64
00:05:07,527 --> 00:05:09,758
So, Allah سبحانه وتعالى revealed the Ayah(آية),

65
00:05:10,353 --> 00:05:19,940
وَقَالُوا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ هَٰذَا الْقُرْآنُ عَلَىٰ رَجُلٍ مِنَ الْقَرْيَتَيْنِ عَظِيمٍ۝

66
00:05:20,571 --> 00:05:27,985
Why wasn't this Qur'an revealed to a great man from one of the two towns,

67
00:05:28,414 --> 00:05:30,853
referring to Makkah and At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف)?

68
00:05:32,144 --> 00:05:35,200
Al-Mugheera Bin Sho'bah(المغيرة بن شعبه), who was from At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف),

69
00:05:35,565 --> 00:05:42,015
he was visiting Makkah, and he said, and this Hadith(حديث) is narrated by Al-Bayhaqi(البيهقي).

70
00:05:42,771 --> 00:05:44,470
Al-Mugheera Bin Sho'bah(المغيرة بن شعبه) said:

71
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:52,996
My first contact with Rasool Allah ﷺ happened one day, when I was walking with Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) in the streets of Makkah

72
00:05:54,092 --> 00:05:56,485
and he ran into Muhammadﷺ.

73
00:05:56,874 --> 00:06:01,347
So, he walked up to us, and he spoke to Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) and said:

74
00:06:02,287 --> 00:06:05,980
Why don't you follow me, believe in Allah believe in Islam.

75
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:08,144
He was giving Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) Daw'ah(دعوة).

76
00:06:09,132 --> 00:06:14,991
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) responded by saying; O Muhammad(محمد), when are you going to stop cursing our gods?

77
00:06:16,077 --> 00:06:20,426
If you want us to testify that you have fulfilled your mission, we will testify for you.

78
00:06:21,443 --> 00:06:27,048
And if I knew that you were telling the truth, I would have already followed you, Muhammadﷺ left.

79
00:06:28,441 --> 00:06:33,265
The meaning of the words of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), if you want us to testify that you have fulfilled the message

80
00:06:33,662 --> 00:06:37,877
because Rasool Allah ﷺ was telling them again and again that my role is to convey a message.

81
00:06:38,485 --> 00:06:41,754
It is not my role to convert you, that is up to Allah.

82
00:06:42,522 --> 00:06:45,539
All what I want to do is to fulfill my mission.

83
00:06:45,769 --> 00:06:50,566
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was saying if you want us to witness for you, in front of Allah we'll do so.

84
00:06:50,873 --> 00:06:54,027
We'll tell Allah that you have done your job, but just leave us alone.

85
00:06:54,658 --> 00:06:57,627
Because if I knew that you were telling the truth, I would have already followed you.

86
00:06:59,301 --> 00:07:00,781
So, Muhammadﷺ left,

87
00:07:01,047 --> 00:07:05,631
AL-Mugheera(المغيره) said: Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) looked at me and said:

88
00:07:05,997 --> 00:07:11,084
I know that he's saying the truth, but there's something holding me back.

89
00:07:12,971 --> 00:07:17,300
The descendants of Qusa'e(قُصَئْ) said: We want to have Hijabah(حِجَابَهْ).

90
00:07:17,593 --> 00:07:21,461
Remember, these are the honors of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

91
00:07:22,022 --> 00:07:24,014
the power and the authority of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

92
00:07:24,038 --> 00:07:27,005
We talked about it, when we talked about Qusa'e Bin Kalaab(قصئ بن كلاب), if you remember

93
00:07:27,583 --> 00:07:32,243
AL-Hijabah(الحجابه) and Siqayah(سقايه), An-Nadwah(اَلنَّدوَةْ), An-Nadwah(اَلنَّدْوَة) means the assembly of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

94
00:07:32,649 --> 00:07:35,036
AL-Hijabah(الحجابه) is the guardianship of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

95
00:07:35,318 --> 00:07:38,621
Sikayah(سقايه) and Rifadah(رفاده) is providing the pilgrims with food and water,

96
00:07:39,188 --> 00:07:40,868
and the Luwaa(اللؤآء) is the banner of war.

97
00:07:41,574 --> 00:07:46,747
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) said: I know that this man is telling the truth, but there's something holding me back,

98
00:07:47,421 --> 00:07:51,946
the descendants of Qusa'e(قُصَئْ) said, we want the authority of An-Nadwah(اَلنَّدوَةْ),

99
00:07:52,254 --> 00:07:53,370
we gave it to them.

100
00:07:54,004 --> 00:07:55,803
We want the authority of AL-Hijabah(الحجابه),

101
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:56,974
we gave it to them.

102
00:07:57,391 --> 00:07:59,292
We want the authority of Luwaa(اَلُّؤآء),

103
00:07:59,518 --> 00:08:00,574
we gave it to them,

104
00:08:00,827 --> 00:08:03,287
we want the authority of Rifadah(رفاده) and Siqayah(سقايه),

105
00:08:03,478 --> 00:08:04,636
we gave it to them.

106
00:08:05,246 --> 00:08:10,893
And now when we started picking up and competing with them, and we were running neck to neck

107
00:08:11,450 --> 00:08:15,990
they came up and say that we have a Prophet among us, how can we compete with that.

108
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:20,218
By God we never gonna accept this.

109
00:08:21,223 --> 00:08:28,774
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) is saying that this is a matter of competition, power struggle between us and the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

110
00:08:29,626 --> 00:08:32,939
They have been given all of the authorities of Makkah.

111
00:08:33,234 --> 00:08:36,234
And now we want to catch up with them, compete with them.

112
00:08:37,715 --> 00:08:42,856
We can't compete with them and providing for the pilgrims and things like that, but we can't compete in Prophet hood.

113
00:08:43,602 --> 00:08:47,445
None of us can compete with the Qur'an that is been given to Muhammadﷺ.

114
00:08:47,612 --> 00:08:49,896
So, we're never going to admit that that's the truth.

115
00:08:50,401 --> 00:08:53,684
Because if we do, that means they would have won against us.

116
00:08:54,026 --> 00:08:56,927
So it's a matter of power, and authority.

117
00:08:57,588 --> 00:09:03,968
So, you can see the element of jealousy and hatred, and not willing to give up power.

118
00:09:04,865 --> 00:09:11,579
And that's why, you would find again and again in Qur'an, that's usually the ones, who are the most outspoken,

119
00:09:12,052 --> 00:09:21,002
and violent in their rejection of the message of the prophets are the ones in authority, the people in power,

120
00:09:21,671 --> 00:09:22,121
Why?

121
00:09:22,161 --> 00:09:26,958
Because they feel that this is a message that will change the status quo

122
00:09:28,096 --> 00:09:35,626
and will strip us from our abilities to take advantages of others and to enslave others.

123
00:09:36,021 --> 00:09:41,220
This is a religion that will free people from worshipping people into worshipping Allah.

124
00:09:42,431 --> 00:09:44,798
And these are referred to in Qur'an as Al-Malaa(ألملاء)

125
00:09:45,948 --> 00:09:49,458
whenever you would have Al-Malaa(ألملاء) in Qur'an it is referring to the leadership.

126
00:09:49,943 --> 00:09:51,568
وَقَالَ الْمَلَأُ مِن قَوْمِه

127
00:09:52,388 --> 00:09:58,126
And this comes up with Firaoun(فرعون) it comes up with the people of Aad(عاد), Salih(صالح) you'd find that it is Al-Malaa(ألملاء).

128
00:09:59,098 --> 00:10:00,733
Ten(10), persecution:

129
00:10:01,519 --> 00:10:10,542
Now, even though Rasool Allah ﷺ was insulted and harmed and false accusations were directed towards him,

130
00:10:11,215 --> 00:10:13,691
he was not persecuted.

131
00:10:14,783 --> 00:10:19,933
And that is part of the protection, of the protection of Allah towards Muhammadﷺ.

132
00:10:20,753 --> 00:10:26,475
Allah سبحانه وتعالى has protected Muhammadﷺ in the early years through his uncle Abu Talib(ابوطالب).

133
00:10:27,725 --> 00:10:33,311
And later on, they would try to assassinate him and Allah سبحانه وتعالى would protect him,

134
00:10:33,351 --> 00:10:35,273
even though his uncle Abu Talib(ابوطالب) has passed away.

135
00:10:36,134 --> 00:10:42,752
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wasn't really persecuted, but it was his followers, who were persecuted.

136
00:10:44,082 --> 00:10:46,430
And this was the opinion of Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ), he states that

137
00:10:46,510 --> 00:10:53,397
he said that Allah has protected Muhammadﷺ because of His love of His messenger.

138
00:10:54,031 --> 00:10:56,934
And Allah has protected him through his uncle Abu Talib(ابوطالب).

139
00:10:57,014 --> 00:10:58,633
These are the words of Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ).

140
00:10:59,892 --> 00:11:07,334
But the persecution of the followers of Rasool Allah ﷺ used to hurt the Messenger of Allah a lot, because he cared about them so much.

141
00:11:08,609 --> 00:11:15,416
And pretty much all of them, went through one form of persecution or another.

142
00:11:16,594 --> 00:11:18,967
In one statement of Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ), he says that

143
00:11:19,427 --> 00:11:22,461
اَلْبَسُوْهُمْ اَدْرَعَلْ حَدِيْدْ وَسَحَرُهُمْ فِيْ الشَّمْسَ

144
00:11:23,190 --> 00:11:27,750
They would wrap them up in shields of iron and leave them in the sun to burn.

145
00:11:28,786 --> 00:11:35,751
So, they would cloth them in shields of iron, steel, and they would leave them in the hot sun of Makkah.

146
00:11:37,052 --> 00:11:46,593
Now, the strongest among the Sahabah(صحابہ), in his response, in fighting the persecution was Bilal Bin Rabbah رضي الله عنه.

147
00:11:47,928 --> 00:11:51,355
The more they would persecute him, the stronger he would become.

148
00:11:52,659 --> 00:12:00,048
He was asked, how come when you were punished, and tortured, you would say Ahad-Ahad(احد احد),

149
00:12:00,801 --> 00:12:02,031
Allah is one, Allah is one.

150
00:12:02,174 --> 00:12:04,886
How come you chose that slogan?

151
00:12:05,650 --> 00:12:09,997
Bilal(بلال) said: Because I found out that, when I would say Ahad-Ahad(احد احد)

152
00:12:10,262 --> 00:12:11,926
it would make them the angriest.

153
00:12:12,672 --> 00:12:15,005
This statement would anger them the most.

154
00:12:16,188 --> 00:12:17,993
And that is why, I would say Ahad-Ahad(احد احد).

155
00:12:18,073 --> 00:12:21,341
So, Bilal(بلال) wasn't looking for a way to reduce the punishment, he didn't care.

156
00:12:22,229 --> 00:12:24,088
And the statement of Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) is

157
00:12:24,168 --> 00:12:25,238
 باعُ نَفْسَه لله

158
00:12:25,461 --> 00:12:29,410
That he sold himself to Allah سبحانه وتعالى, he gave up his life to Allah.

159
00:12:30,413 --> 00:12:33,816
He would say Ahad-Ahad(احد احد) and Umayyah Bin Khalaf(اميه بن خلف) would become angry

160
00:12:34,175 --> 00:12:40,222
and would add the punishment, and Bilal(بلال) would only say it louder, wouldn't give up.

161
00:12:41,335 --> 00:12:44,559
Now they went through different forms of torture.

162
00:12:45,025 --> 00:12:48,245
And the torture was not only limited to the slaves and servants

163
00:12:48,572 --> 00:12:50,981
but even some of the nobility were tortured.

164
00:12:51,124 --> 00:12:57,629
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان بن عفان), belonging to one of the noblest families of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), Bannu Umayyah(بَنُو اُمَيَّه),

165
00:12:58,089 --> 00:13:05,781
 he was wrapped in a carpet and then they would jump over him and crush him inside that carpet.

166
00:13:07,230 --> 00:13:11,014
And you're familiar with some of the stories of persecution that happened to the slaves.

167
00:13:11,554 --> 00:13:16,159
Like what happened to Sumayyah(سميه), and her husband and her son,

168
00:13:16,723 --> 00:13:22,939
Yasser(ياسر), and Sumayyah(سميه) were both killed, under the severe tormenting of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

169
00:13:23,787 --> 00:13:29,916
In one narration, it states that Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) struck Sumayyah(سميه) with a spear in her private parts, until he killed her.

170
00:13:31,341 --> 00:13:36,981
And all of this was becoming so much on Sayyedina Ammar رضي الله عنه,

171
00:13:37,346 --> 00:13:43,073
it's a combination of psychological pain and physical pain,

172
00:13:43,899 --> 00:13:46,701
physical pain because of the tormenting was going through.

173
00:13:47,145 --> 00:13:53,852
Plus seeing his mother and father go through this severe punishment and sad ending.

174
00:13:54,605 --> 00:14:01,970
 Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر) buckled under this pressure and he spoke some words against Muhammadﷺ.

175
00:14:03,322 --> 00:14:14,113
Now, when he woke up from the pain, he went to Rasool Allahﷺ, sad and sorry for what has happened

176
00:14:14,153 --> 00:14:17,652
and he narrated the incident to Muhammadﷺ.

177
00:14:18,763 --> 00:14:22,447
Allah سبحانه وتعالى revealed an Ayah(آية) dealing with that particular situation,

178
00:14:23,733 --> 00:14:34,382
saying that one is excused to speak some words with the tongue, under this torture if the heart is confident with faith,

179
00:14:34,865 --> 00:14:43,603
if the heart is firm on Eeman(ايمان) and has Yaqeen(يقين) it is ok for a person to speak,

180
00:14:44,443 --> 00:14:45,222
because

181
00:14:45,254 --> 00:14:46,952
 لَا يُكَلِّفُ اللَّهُ نَفْسًا إِلَّا وُسْعَهَا ۚ

182
00:14:46,992 --> 00:14:49,295
Allah سبحانه وتعالى does not overburden a person.

183
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:54,097
This is unbearable pain that Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر) was going through.

184
00:14:56,078 --> 00:15:01,689
So, this persecution continued with almost all of the Sahabah(صحابہ) with a few exceptions,

185
00:15:01,769 --> 00:15:10,279
the ones who had some strong backing of their families and had some sympathy from some of their non believing relatives.

186
00:15:10,922 --> 00:15:20,416
Now the severest in his punishment and the one who would actually mobilize the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), was Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

187
00:15:21,278 --> 00:15:23,197
He was their leader in evil,

188
00:15:23,697 --> 00:15:30,859
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) states: "that sinner Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was the one, who incited the men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) against them.

189
00:15:31,716 --> 00:15:35,380
When he heard of a man of status and influence who had accepted Islam.

190
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:42,775
He would upbraid and insult him saying, you have abandoned the religion of your father, a man better than you.

191
00:15:43,731 --> 00:15:52,209
We will depreciate your values, deride your opinions and destroy your reputation.

192
00:15:53,035 --> 00:15:59,610
If the Muslim were merchant, he would say we will by God boycott doing business with you, and we will ruin you.

193
00:16:00,185 --> 00:16:05,853
If the Muslim was defenseless Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) would beat him up and incite others against him,

194
00:16:06,078 --> 00:16:08,121
may Allah damn and punishment him.

195
00:16:09,424 --> 00:16:16,889
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was the spear head of the efforts of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) against the Muslims in Makkah.

196
00:16:18,365 --> 00:16:19,524
Number 11:

197
00:16:19,873 --> 00:16:21,555
Forgot to mention Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

198
00:16:22,214 --> 00:16:27,885
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), he had a slave girl that he would torture,

199
00:16:28,952 --> 00:16:31,602
and sometimes he would stop.

200
00:16:32,293 --> 00:16:36,461
And to show you, his personality, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) when he would stop,

201
00:16:36,959 --> 00:16:41,652
he would tell her, don't think that I'm giving you a break because I'm having sympathy on you.

202
00:16:41,888 --> 00:16:44,618
The only reason why I stopped is because I'm tired.

203
00:16:45,936 --> 00:16:47,368
Otherwise I would continue.

204
00:16:48,032 --> 00:16:48,207
But

205
00:16:48,247 --> 00:16:49,572
الله سبحانه وتعالى يَهْدِيْ مَنْ يَشَاءْ

206
00:16:49,612 --> 00:16:51,540
Allah سبحانه وتعالى guides whomever He wills.

207
00:16:52,187 --> 00:16:59,307
11) When the attempts of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) of character assassinations failed.

208
00:16:59,992 --> 00:17:02,286
They attempted to assassinate the character.

209
00:17:03,317 --> 00:17:10,921
They tried to destroy the message by distorting the image of the messenger.

210
00:17:12,199 --> 00:17:16,929
When that didn't work, they tried to eliminate the Messenger.

211
00:17:18,036 --> 00:17:21,584
And these attempts occurred after Abu Talib(ابوطالب) passed away.

212
00:17:22,247 --> 00:17:27,981
They knew that they have no way of assassinating Muhammadﷺ during the life of Abu Talib(ابوطالب).

213
00:17:29,236 --> 00:17:32,848
But when he passed away, they attempted to assassinate him.

214
00:17:33,507 --> 00:17:35,054
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى says,

215
00:17:35,336 --> 00:17:43,357
وَإِذْ يَمْكُرُ بِكَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لِيُثْبِتُوكَ أَوْ يَقْتُلُوكَ أَوْ يُخْرِجُوكَ ۚ

216
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:50,247
وَيَمْكُرُونَ وَيَمْكُرُ اللَّهُ ۖ وَاللَّهُ خَيْرُ الْمَاكِرِينَ۝

217
00:17:50,819 --> 00:17:59,169
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says they attempted to drive you out of your land, to imprison you and to kill you.

218
00:17:59,884 --> 00:18:02,444
So, the attempts were made but Allah سبحانه وتعالى would protect him,

219
00:18:02,484 --> 00:18:06,885
and we'll talk about one of these attempts when we talk about Hijrah(هجرة).

220
00:18:07,818 --> 00:18:15,306
So, these are the various methods that the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) used at one time or another during the era of Makkah.

221
00:18:16,292 --> 00:18:20,637
What was the response of Rasool Allahﷺ, how would he respond to all of this?

222
00:18:22,029 --> 00:18:28,061
In Al-Bukhari(اَلبُخَارِي), Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت), who was one of the Sahabah(صحابہ) who went through a lot.

223
00:18:29,021 --> 00:18:36,372
He went to Rasool Allah ﷺ while the Messenger of Allah was leaning his back towards the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

224
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:39,299
And he walked up to Muhammadﷺ and said,

225
00:18:39,354 --> 00:18:43,608
يَا رَسُوْل الله اَلَا تَدْعُ لَنَا ، اَلَا تَسْتَنْصِرُلَنَا

226
00:18:44,801 --> 00:18:48,958
O Messenger of Allah, Why don't you make Dua(دُعَا) for us?

227
00:18:49,537 --> 00:18:50,723
 That's all what he said.

228
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:54,856
But the message implies that we are going through a lot.

229
00:18:55,641 --> 00:19:00,144
Why don't you ask Allah to ease the pain that we're going through.

230
00:19:01,104 --> 00:19:04,004
And Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت) was going through a lot himself.

231
00:19:04,318 --> 00:19:07,107
One day later on, when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was the Khalifah(خليفه),

232
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:14,123
Umar(عُمَر) was asking all of the people around to talk about their experiences in Makkah.

233
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:15,968
What did you go through?

234
00:19:16,359 --> 00:19:21,038
So, when the term came on Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت), he didn't speak.

235
00:19:21,782 --> 00:19:27,336
All what he did was, lift his shirt and expose his back. That's it!

236
00:19:28,032 --> 00:19:31,624
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) Said: I have never seen something like this.

237
00:19:32,054 --> 00:19:33,244
What happened to you?

238
00:19:33,684 --> 00:19:41,089
Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت) had deep holes, deep black holes in his back.

239
00:19:42,061 --> 00:19:48,862
He said when I was in Makkah, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) would bring some rocks and burn them over fire,

240
00:19:49,092 --> 00:19:54,236
some small rocks and they would burn them on fire until they turn red.

241
00:19:54,795 --> 00:20:02,898
And then they would lay them on the hot sand in the desert of Makkah, and they would throw me on top of it.

242
00:20:03,588 --> 00:20:07,716
So, these rocks, they would burn through my flesh

243
00:20:08,194 --> 00:20:16,349
and I would hear the burning of my flesh and I would smell my fat, grease is burning.

244
00:20:16,626 --> 00:20:20,326
 He said: I would smell the smoke coming off from my back.

245
00:20:21,634 --> 00:20:25,637
So, Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت) had something to complain about.

246
00:20:26,330 --> 00:20:30,961
This was severe pain that he was going through, and all what he asked for is

247
00:20:31,052 --> 00:20:33,157
يَا رَسُوْل الله ، اَلَا تَسْتَنْصِرُلَنَا

248
00:20:33,197 --> 00:20:36,371
O Rasool Ullah, why don't you ask Allah to give us victory?

249
00:20:37,742 --> 00:20:40,046
What was the response of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

250
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:45,611
Rasool Allah ﷺ he sat straight and his face turned red

251
00:20:45,826 --> 00:20:48,947
and that would happen to Rasool Allah ﷺ, when he would become angry.

252
00:20:49,953 --> 00:20:51,077
And then he said,

253
00:20:51,688 --> 00:20:53,823
كَانَ يُؤتى بِمَنْ قَبْلَكُمْ

254
00:20:54,291 --> 00:20:58,026
فَيُنْشَرْ الْمِنْشَارُ الْحَدِيدِ مَا بَيْنَ لَحْمِهِ أَوْ عَصَبِهِ وَ عَظَمِهِ،

255
00:20:58,592 --> 00:21:00,666
 فَلَا يَرُدَّه’ ذَلِكَ عَنْ دِينِهِ،

256
00:21:01,238 --> 00:21:08,368
فَكَانَ يوتى بِاَحَدٍ فَيُوضَعُ الْمِنْشَارُ عَلَى مَفْرِقِ رَأْسِهِ فَيُشَقُّ بنصفين، فَلَا يَدَعُ دِينَه

257
00:21:09,110 --> 00:21:15,627
وَلَيُتِمَّنَّ اللَّهُ هَذَا الأَمْرَ حَتَّى يَسِيرَ الرَّاكِبُ مِنْ صَنْعَاءَ إِلَى حَضْرَمَوْتَ،لَا يَخَافُ إِلاَّ اللَّهَ وَالذِّئْبَ عَلَى غَنَمِهِ

258
00:21:16,542 --> 00:21:23,205
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: A believer among those who were before you, used to be combed with iron combs

259
00:21:23,602 --> 00:21:27,942
that would separate the flesh and nerves from their bones.

260
00:21:28,404 --> 00:21:35,074
So, you'd have iron combs, and they would comb the flesh of their bones.

261
00:21:36,257 --> 00:21:38,407
But they would never desert their religion.

262
00:21:39,383 --> 00:21:45,375
And they would bring one of them and place a saw on top of their heads,

263
00:21:46,157 --> 00:21:48,766
and they would be cut into two halves.

264
00:21:49,631 --> 00:21:52,218
And yet they would never give up their religion.

265
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:56,631
In the name of Allah, Allah will give His religion victory,

266
00:21:57,268 --> 00:22:03,568
until a traveler will go from Sana'a(صنعاء) all the way to Hazaral Maot(حضرموت), fearing no one but Allah.

267
00:22:04,943 --> 00:22:06,729
What can we learn from this Hadith(حديث).?

268
00:22:07,348 --> 00:22:11,427
Number one, Rasool Allah ﷺ is asking us to be patient.

269
00:22:12,397 --> 00:22:17,500
Be patient, even if you are going through a lot, be patient never give up,

270
00:22:18,971 --> 00:22:23,523
All what Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت) was going through, still Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling him be patient.

271
00:22:24,771 --> 00:22:29,128
The second lesson, Allahسبحانه وتعالى has some laws,

272
00:22:29,583 --> 00:22:33,451
just like there are laws in nature, there are laws of history,

273
00:22:33,773 --> 00:22:37,875
there are laws of sociology, there are laws of psychology,

274
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:41,256
and there are laws in the establishment of religion.

275
00:22:41,697 --> 00:22:47,388
And you will have to go through the stages and Allahسبحانه وتعالى will not give you an exception

276
00:22:47,806 --> 00:22:50,981
you will have to go through what the nation's before you, went through.

277
00:22:51,788 --> 00:22:53,242
This is what they went through.

278
00:22:54,282 --> 00:23:00,715
The same will happen with you and Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted his Ummah(امة) to be the best of nations.

279
00:23:01,364 --> 00:23:05,101
If the people before were patient, I want my Ummah(امة) to be more patient.

280
00:23:06,070 --> 00:23:09,310
If the people before were strong, I want my people to be stronger.

281
00:23:09,879 --> 00:23:11,832
And that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ was angry.

282
00:23:12,409 --> 00:23:15,692
He wants the best to be in his Ummah(امة).

283
00:23:16,372 --> 00:23:18,760
He wants his Ummah(امة) to show the best example.

284
00:23:19,078 --> 00:23:21,952
He wants to be proud with us on the Day of Judgment.

285
00:23:22,428 --> 00:23:28,753
Therefore, dear brothers or sisters, we have to live up to what Rasool Allah ﷺ expects from us.

286
00:23:29,372 --> 00:23:34,077
He wants to meet us on the day of Judgment and see us and he wants to be proud with us.

287
00:23:34,498 --> 00:23:36,751
And Rasool Allah ﷺ has stated this in a few Ahadith(احاديث).

288
00:23:37,557 --> 00:23:40,042
For example, in one Hadith(حديث) Rasool Allah ﷺ says:

289
00:23:40,217 --> 00:23:46,182
I want you to get married and to multiply, because I want to be proud with your numbers on the Day of Judgment.

290
00:23:46,582 --> 00:23:48,312
He even wants to be proud with our numbers.

291
00:23:48,471 --> 00:23:53,792
So he's asking us to have a lot of kids, and he's asking us to get married.

292
00:23:54,393 --> 00:23:56,398
 And Rasool Allah ﷺ in another Hadith(حديث),

293
00:23:57,116 --> 00:24:01,939
I saw a huge nation in front of my eyes.

294
00:24:02,732 --> 00:24:06,298
So, I asked the angels who are accompanying me, Is this my Ummah(امة)?

295
00:24:06,803 --> 00:24:10,689
They said: No, this is not your Ummah(امة); this is the Ummah(امة) of Musa(موسى), these are Banni Israel(بني اسرائيل).

296
00:24:11,538 --> 00:24:16,334
So, Banni Israel(بني اسرائيل) is the second largest Ummah(امة) after the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ, it's a huge numbers.

297
00:24:16,762 --> 00:24:20,085
So, the greatest Ummah(امة) after the Ummah(امة) of Muhammadﷺ is the children of Israel(اسرائيل)

298
00:24:21,207 --> 00:24:23,587
And then the Angels told me: Look at your right side.

299
00:24:23,990 --> 00:24:28,128
So, I looked and I saw people filling the horizon.

300
00:24:28,695 --> 00:24:33,438
They told me look at the left side and I looked and I saw people filling the horizon.

301
00:24:34,335 --> 00:24:42,977
The angels told me, this is your Ummah(امة), in addition to them, Allah will give you 70,000, who will enter Paradise without going through reckoning.

302
00:24:43,497 --> 00:24:49,403
Rasool Allah ﷺ said in another narration of the Hadith(حديث), that I was very impressed by their looks.

303
00:24:50,183 --> 00:24:52,766
I was so impressed by their looks, I was proud

304
00:24:53,385 --> 00:24:57,792
and the interpreters of the Hadith(حديث), the commentators of the Hadith(حديث) said,

305
00:24:57,917 --> 00:25:02,678
Rasool Allah ﷺ was impressed because he saw on them, the signs of Sujood(سجود) and Wudhoo(وضؤ)

306
00:25:04,074 --> 00:25:06,866
and that made light shine out of their faces.

307
00:25:07,273 --> 00:25:12,650
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ loves this, he loves to see his Ummah(امة) in the best shape and form.

308
00:25:13,632 --> 00:25:19,559
So, he is telling Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب ابن ارت), you have to be patient, this is what happened to the people before.

309
00:25:19,749 --> 00:25:24,535
You have to go through that, and you have to show a better example.

310
00:25:25,495 --> 00:25:27,078
Third lesson, to be learned.

311
00:25:27,821 --> 00:25:30,817
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Allah will complete His religion

312
00:25:31,650 --> 00:25:38,824
until a traveler will leave from Sana'a(صنعاء) all the way to Hazaral Maot(حضر موت) fearing no one but Allah.

313
00:25:40,046 --> 00:25:43,133
How come Rasool Allah ﷺ chose Sana'a(صنعاء) and Hazaral Maot(حضر موت).?

314
00:25:43,213 --> 00:25:44,319
Rasool Allah was in Makkah

315
00:25:44,865 --> 00:25:50,624
why didn't he use Makkah as a reference point, since they were insecure.?

316
00:25:51,060 --> 00:25:55,534
How cannot speak about their insecurity, how come Rasool Allah ﷺ is bringing an example from Yemen?

317
00:25:55,724 --> 00:25:57,780
Both Sana'a(صنعاء) and Hazaral Maot(حضر موت) are in Yemen.

318
00:25:58,121 --> 00:26:02,867
Now since this relates to somebody who's going so in security in Makkah,

319
00:26:03,041 --> 00:26:08,643
how came Rasool Allah ﷺ didn't say Makkah and Madina, Makkah and Hajar(هَجَر), Makkah and Syria.

320
00:26:09,752 --> 00:26:12,955
Or how come he didn't choose two reference points in another country?

321
00:26:13,272 --> 00:26:14,819
How come Sana'a(صنعاء) and Hazaral Maot(حضر موت)?

322
00:26:15,423 --> 00:26:21,075
There's something interesting in the choice of Rasool Allah ﷺ of these particular two areas in Yemen.

323
00:26:22,156 --> 00:26:26,434
Yemen used to be and still is, a very tribal society.

324
00:26:27,267 --> 00:26:37,781
And in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ all of that area was covered by armed tribes, who had constant war between them.

325
00:26:38,835 --> 00:26:43,589
And they were in rivalry and it was insecure.

326
00:26:44,506 --> 00:26:52,547
When Islam entered into Yemen, during the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ Islam made the whole area peaceful.

327
00:26:53,214 --> 00:27:00,420
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) now, when people are getting away from Islam, and we're missing the Islamic rule,

328
00:27:01,126 --> 00:27:07,839
that same area between Sana'a(صنعاء) and Hazaral Maot(حضر موت) today is one of the most insecure areas in Yemen.

329
00:27:08,505 --> 00:27:14,826
And if somebody wants to travel through a particular route that will go through the tribal areas

330
00:27:15,177 --> 00:27:20,605
between Sana'a(صنعاء) and Hazaral Maot(حزرالموت) forget about traveling, if you are not armed.

331
00:27:21,764 --> 00:27:26,526
So it's, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) very interesting that Rasool Allah ﷺ chose this area,

332
00:27:27,094 --> 00:27:36,015
which is now one of the more insecure areas in the world as a reference, to say that you cannot have peace without Islam.

333
00:27:36,372 --> 00:27:38,061
And this leads to the fifth lesson

334
00:27:38,455 --> 00:27:42,955
that there is no comprehensive peace unless Islam reigns.

335
00:27:44,392 --> 00:27:47,617
Under Islam, people will have true peace.

336
00:27:48,081 --> 00:27:50,621
And that's the meaning of the word Islam, peace.

337
00:27:52,128 --> 00:28:01,063
Another example that could reveal to us how Rasool Allah ﷺ used to deal with these situations of people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

338
00:28:01,789 --> 00:28:04,003
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), met together and said,

339
00:28:04,099 --> 00:28:13,294
Let's find somebody who's the most experts in poetry and magic, to go and meet Muhammadﷺ and tell us how to deal with him.

340
00:28:14,730 --> 00:28:21,177
So, they decided that they're going to send Utba Bin Rabiya(عتبة بن ربيعه), who was supposedly an expert in these areas.

341
00:28:22,708 --> 00:28:30,093
Utba Bin Rabiya(عتبة بن ربيعه), he went to Muhammadﷺ and said tell me, O Muhammad(محمد), who is better, you or Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).

342
00:28:31,033 --> 00:28:36,960
These questions are a setup, in the society of Arabia.

343
00:28:37,946 --> 00:28:42,850
They had so much respect and glorification for their ancestry.

344
00:28:43,697 --> 00:28:48,098
And the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ was a lineage of nobility.

345
00:28:48,856 --> 00:28:56,642
So, these were, held in very high esteem, not only among the family of Rasool Allah, but among everyone in Makkah.

346
00:28:57,841 --> 00:29:04,104
Qusa'e Bin Kulaab(قصئ بن كلاب), Hashim(هاشم), Abdul Muttalib(عبدالمطلب), these were people, who were glorified.

347
00:29:05,084 --> 00:29:08,036
And forget about speaking against any one of them.

348
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:12,640
You just can't do that; It's not allowed, unaccepted, not tolerated.

349
00:29:13,889 --> 00:29:21,710
So Utba(عتبة), who is not a descendant of Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) is asking Muhammadﷺ,

350
00:29:22,671 --> 00:29:26,547
What do you say about your father Abdullah(عبدالله), tell us what, what's your opinion about him?

351
00:29:27,472 --> 00:29:30,230
What do you say about your grandfather Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب)?

352
00:29:31,398 --> 00:29:32,898
These were setup questions.

353
00:29:33,668 --> 00:29:37,168
He asked him about Abdullah(عبدالله).? Rasool Allah ﷺ remained silent, he didn't answer.

354
00:29:37,795 --> 00:29:40,997
He asked him about Abdul Muttalib(عبد المطلب).? Rasool Allah ﷺ did not respond.

355
00:29:41,139 --> 00:29:50,298
So, Utbah(عتبه) said: If you claim those men to be better than you the fact is they worship the gods you have criticized.

356
00:29:51,827 --> 00:29:56,575
If you claim to be better than them, then speak so we can hear what you say.

357
00:29:57,655 --> 00:30:02,931
By God, we've never seen any fool more harmful to his people than you.

358
00:30:03,583 --> 00:30:08,691
You've caused division and dissension among us, criticized our religion

359
00:30:08,935 --> 00:30:17,751
and so disgraced us in the eyes of the Arabs, that the rumor is current among them, that there is a magician or a sorcerer, amidst Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

360
00:30:18,692 --> 00:30:24,744
Now Utbah(عتبه) is blaming Muhammadﷺ for this rumor, that there is a sorcerer in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

361
00:30:25,045 --> 00:30:27,831
Who founded, this rumor start with?

362
00:30:28,487 --> 00:30:34,444
Who is the one, who went around telling the people that there's a sorcerer among us isn't that the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and among them Utbah(عتبة)

363
00:30:34,924 --> 00:30:38,694
and now he's blaming Muhammadﷺ for it, because it affected them,

364
00:30:39,202 --> 00:30:41,091
 and it was an embarrassment for them.

365
00:30:41,352 --> 00:30:46,195
They are the ones, who told the Arabs that he's a sorcerer and now it's an embarrassment for them.

366
00:30:46,570 --> 00:30:51,877
Everyone among the other tribes are speaking about the sorcerer among Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

367
00:30:52,274 --> 00:30:53,607
Then he said;

368
00:30:54,326 --> 00:31:04,544
By God, fellow it seems all we have to await, is the cry of a pregnant woman for us all to be at one another with swords, till we wipe ourselves out.

369
00:31:04,954 --> 00:31:09,002
What he meant by this is, we're waiting for the cry of a pregnant woman meaning,

370
00:31:09,280 --> 00:31:15,714
in a very short time, we might be fighting each other in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), because of what you have brought?

371
00:31:16,238 --> 00:31:20,960
 You have caused disunity among us, we are about to jump at each other's throats.

372
00:31:22,555 --> 00:31:25,365
And then he offered him similar offers.

373
00:31:25,698 --> 00:31:32,238
What do you want status or wealth, whatever you want, we'll give it to you just tell us so that we can bring an end to this.

374
00:31:32,893 --> 00:31:38,046
Rasool Allah ﷺ allowed Utbah(عتبة) to go on, with this nonsense, without interrupting him.

375
00:31:38,528 --> 00:31:40,606
Rasool Allah ﷺ was a very good listener.

376
00:31:41,177 --> 00:31:45,502
Even though all of this was stuff that didn't make any sense.

377
00:31:45,630 --> 00:31:48,114
Rasool Allah ﷺ was calmly listening.

378
00:31:48,924 --> 00:31:55,058
And when Utbah(عتبة) finished, Rasool Allah ﷺ asked him: O Utbah(عتبة), are you done?

379
00:31:55,978 --> 00:31:59,383
Very kindly, are you done? He said: Yes.

380
00:32:00,657 --> 00:32:06,930
Rasool Allah ﷺ, did not respond to what he was saying by his own words.

381
00:32:07,496 --> 00:32:10,944
But he started reciting Ayaat(آيات) from Surah Al-Fusilat(سورة الفصلت).

382
00:32:11,837 --> 00:32:12,513
In the beginning,

383
00:32:12,553 --> 00:32:13,661
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ۝

384
00:32:13,968 --> 00:32:16,679
In the Name of God, the Most Merciful and beneficent

385
00:32:17,731 --> 00:32:22,368
حم ۝

386
00:32:22,694 --> 00:32:28,649
تَنْزِيلٌ مِنَ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ ۝

387
00:32:29,103 --> 00:32:38,716
كِتَابٌ فُصِّلَتْ آيَاتُهُ قُرْآنًا عَرَبِيًّا لِقَوْمٍ يَعْلَمُونَ۝

388
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:43,660
Ha(ح), Meem(م), A revelation from the Most Merciful and Beneficent,

389
00:32:44,510 --> 00:32:50,615
a book whose verses have been detailed in an Arabic Qur'an for people who are aware,

390
00:32:51,377 --> 00:32:55,553
and he went on going on and on it's about the page, quite a few Ayaat(آيات).

391
00:32:56,210 --> 00:32:59,408
And he kept on reciting until he reached to a verse that states,

392
00:33:00,003 --> 00:33:06,100
I warn you of a terrible punishment like that which destroyed Aad(عاد) and Thamood(ثمود).

393
00:33:07,029 --> 00:33:12,979
In one narration, it says that when Rasool Allah ﷺ, mentioned this Ayah(آية).

394
00:33:13,179 --> 00:33:18,175
Utbah(عتبة) placed his hand over the mouth of Rasool Allah ﷺ and urged him to stop.

395
00:33:19,374 --> 00:33:21,849
Because this Ayah(آية) is threatening them with punishment.

396
00:33:22,529 --> 00:33:26,686
And Utbah(عتبة) knew deep in his heart that Muhammadﷺ is truthful,

397
00:33:27,049 --> 00:33:29,460
he never said, anything that did not come to happen

398
00:33:29,927 --> 00:33:34,154
and if he is threatening us with punishment, it might come to happen.

399
00:33:34,400 --> 00:33:39,544
So, I need to stop him and he said, I asked you in the name of the relationship between us to stop.

400
00:33:40,203 --> 00:33:45,681
And in this other narration, it states that Utbah(عتبة), went back to the people and they told them what happened.

401
00:33:45,744 --> 00:33:50,260
He said, he recited to me Qur'an and I did not understand anything he was saying,

402
00:33:50,441 --> 00:33:54,543
except that he threatened us with a punishment like the punishment of Aad(عاد) and Thamood(ثمود),

403
00:33:55,248 --> 00:33:59,100
they told him; Woe to you, he's speaking to you in Arabic and you don't understand him.

404
00:33:59,499 --> 00:34:02,769
He said; In the name of Allah I did not understand, what he was talking about.

405
00:34:03,189 --> 00:34:09,774
 Well, the same Ayaat(آيات) say that some people have a seal over their heart, they will not understand it.

406
00:34:10,642 --> 00:34:15,893
The lesson to learn from this is that Rasool Allah ﷺ dealt with different situations, different ways.

407
00:34:16,801 --> 00:34:23,066
And many times he would use Qur'an to respond to what they were saying.

408
00:34:24,032 --> 00:34:28,389
So, let's use Qur'an, let's use the concepts of Qur'an in our Da'wah(دعوة).

409
00:34:29,115 --> 00:34:31,755
What is better to use, than the words of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ.

410
00:34:32,959 --> 00:34:36,358
I'll talk about the story of the Dimaadh(ضماد),

411
00:34:37,088 --> 00:34:44,535
Dimaadh Al-Asdi(ضماد الازدي) was a man from Azd-Shinwaa( أَزْدِ شَنُوءَةَ ) from Southern Arabia, he came into Makkah.

412
00:34:45,245 --> 00:34:55,141
And he heard some of the people in Makkah saying that there is a man among us, who was obsessed with Jin(جن).

413
00:34:55,952 --> 00:34:57,943
They were referring to Muhammadﷺ.

414
00:34:58,721 --> 00:35:04,907
Dimaadh Al-Asdi(ضماد الازدي) used to be a man, who would heal people, who are obsessed with demons.

415
00:35:05,438 --> 00:35:11,732
So, with the right intentions, Dimaadh Al-Asdi(ضماد الازدي) went to Rasool Allah ﷺ to offer his help.

416
00:35:12,286 --> 00:35:16,706
He didn't mean anything bad, I mean, he never met Rasool Allah ﷺ, he doesn't know him.

417
00:35:17,166 --> 00:35:19,024
Since he was an expert healer,

418
00:35:19,283 --> 00:35:26,647
he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: I heard that you are obsessed with Jin(جن) and I'm offering my service, if you want I can help you.

419
00:35:27,831 --> 00:35:33,375
Which is a quite an insulting statement, but Rasool Allahﷺ, was a very compassionate

420
00:35:33,430 --> 00:35:38,311
 and he understood that this man might have heard some wrong information.

421
00:35:38,908 --> 00:35:43,575
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ started by mentioning the words of Khut'ba-Tul-Haajah(خطبة الحاجة)

422
00:35:43,981 --> 00:35:47,352
إِنَّ الْحَمْدَ لِلهِ، نَحْمدُهُ ونَسْتَعينُهُ وَنَسْتَغْفِرُهُ وَنَسْتَهْدِيْ،

423
00:35:47,599 --> 00:35:50,757
وَنَعُوذُ باللهِ مِنْ شرورِ أَنْفُسِنَا وسَيِّئَاتِ أَعْمَالِنَا،

424
00:35:50,987 --> 00:35:54,149
مَنْ يَهْدِهِ اللهُ فَلَا مُضِلَّ لَهُ، وَمَنْ يُضْلِلْ فَلَا هَادِيَ لَهُ

425
00:35:54,358 --> 00:36:01,842
These are the words Rasool Allah ﷺ would usually start with, he would use these words as an opening of his speech.

426
00:36:02,263 --> 00:36:04,317
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ just started with these words.

427
00:36:05,065 --> 00:36:09,859
Let me translate them, Praise be to God, we praise Him and seek His help

428
00:36:10,326 --> 00:36:14,156
whomever God leads a right! No one can lead astray.

429
00:36:14,604 --> 00:36:18,016
Whomever God leads astray! No one can lead a right.

430
00:36:18,435 --> 00:36:24,391
I bear testimony that there is no God but Allah alone, who has no associates.

431
00:36:25,236 --> 00:36:32,293
The words in Arabic obviously have a rhyme to them and are quite eloquent, you lose that in translation.

432
00:36:32,643 --> 00:36:37,647
But anyway, Dimaadh(ضماد) interrupted Rasool Allah ﷺ, he stopped him.

433
00:36:38,985 --> 00:36:43,045
And he said: O, Muhammad(محمد), can you please repeat those words again.

434
00:36:43,522 --> 00:36:45,621
Rasool Allah ﷺ repeated them again.

435
00:36:46,105 --> 00:36:49,716
Dimaadh(ضماد) said; I have never heard something like this.

436
00:36:50,224 --> 00:36:55,371
These words are so wonderful, they are going to reach the depths of the ocean,

437
00:36:55,451 --> 00:36:57,609
meaning these words are going to have influence.

438
00:36:59,135 --> 00:37:03,412
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, then pledge allegiance to me,

439
00:37:04,118 --> 00:37:05,458
اُمدِدْ يَدَكَ اُبَايعكْ

440
00:37:05,968 --> 00:37:06,939
Become a Muslim.

441
00:37:07,247 --> 00:37:08,867
He immediately extended his hand and said:

442
00:37:08,907 --> 00:37:12,179
 اشهد ان لا إله إلا الله وأشهد ان محمد رسول الله

443
00:37:12,369 --> 00:37:16,112
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: How about you also pledged for your people, your tribe.

444
00:37:16,434 --> 00:37:18,665
 He said: and I will pledge for my people.

445
00:37:19,580 --> 00:37:24,253
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) here you have a man, coming with one objective,

446
00:37:24,908 --> 00:37:28,003
meeting Rasool Allah ﷺ for a few minutes, leaving as a Muslim.

447
00:37:28,983 --> 00:37:32,045
He came to heal Rasool Allah ﷺ, Rasool Allah ﷺ healed him.

448
00:37:32,649 --> 00:37:36,402
He went and left after this short meeting as a Muslim.

449
00:37:36,753 --> 00:37:43,200
That was the personality that Rasool Allah ﷺ had, he had so much presence, so much influence on people

450
00:37:43,423 --> 00:37:49,106
that within a short meeting it completely changes their lives.

451
00:37:49,905 --> 00:37:53,735
I mean, this is a life changing event for Dimaadh(ضماد), becoming a Muslim.

452
00:37:53,996 --> 00:37:55,581
It occurred within one meeting.

453
00:37:56,088 --> 00:38:03,209
And this is a leadership quality that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has given Muhammadﷺ, he had this ability to influence others.

454
00:38:04,495 --> 00:38:12,324
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) years later, Rasool Allah ﷺ sent an army that passed next to the village of Dimaadh(ضماد).

455
00:38:13,102 --> 00:38:17,447
The leader of the army, asked them did you take anything from these people.

456
00:38:17,800 --> 00:38:23,514
So, one soldier in the army said: Yes, I have taken away from them, a strong camel.

457
00:38:24,063 --> 00:38:28,006
The leader of the army said: Give it back because these are the people of Dimaadh(ضماد).

458
00:38:28,507 --> 00:38:32,670
And Rasool Allah ﷺ has given them protection, give them back what belongs to them.

459
00:38:33,222 --> 00:38:36,985
Another story with is a man called Amr Bin Absaa(عمرو بن عبسه),

460
00:38:37,089 --> 00:38:41,827
Amr Bin Absaa(عمرو بن عبسه) was a man from Arabia, he wasn't from Makkah,

461
00:38:42,429 --> 00:38:44,572
Amr Bin Absaa(عمرو بن عبسه) speaks about himself.

462
00:38:44,652 --> 00:38:46,618
He mentions his story, it's in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

463
00:38:47,182 --> 00:38:51,202
 He says, In the time of Jahilliyah(جاهليه), in the time of ignorance,

464
00:38:52,155 --> 00:38:57,540
I had belief in my heart, that the religion of my people is false.

465
00:38:58,532 --> 00:39:05,399
And I had no trust or belief in worshipping idols, I knew deep in my heart that this is wrong.

466
00:39:05,969 --> 00:39:12,310
And then one day I came to know, that there was a man in Makkah, preaching a new religion.

467
00:39:12,989 --> 00:39:16,581
So, I immediately went on my camel to meet him.

468
00:39:17,854 --> 00:39:24,424
So, I came in, and Watalaftu(وَتَلَطَّفْتُ)  He said: I had to sneak in and secretly meet him.

469
00:39:24,487 --> 00:39:32,297
That was how difficult the conditions were in Makkah, that a person from outside Makkah cannot meet Rasool Allah ﷺ publicly.

470
00:39:32,725 --> 00:39:37,711
You can't even meet him, he said, Watalaftu(وَتَلَطَّفْتُ) I had to do it secretly.

471
00:39:38,284 --> 00:39:41,679
And then I came to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ, I told him, What are you.?

472
00:39:42,293 --> 00:39:43,536
He said, I'm a Prophet.

473
00:39:44,165 --> 00:39:45,689
He said: What does that mean?

474
00:39:46,649 --> 00:39:49,149
He said: I was sent by Allah.

475
00:39:49,912 --> 00:39:51,533
What did he send you with?

476
00:39:52,157 --> 00:39:55,293
And you can notice the simplicity of the Bedouin.

477
00:39:55,526 --> 00:40:00,909
The mind is not complicated with philosophy and arguments and very simple.

478
00:40:00,949 --> 00:40:02,392
What are you? I'm a Prophet.

479
00:40:02,710 --> 00:40:03,964
What does that mean?

480
00:40:04,638 --> 00:40:06,250
It means that I was sent by Allah.

481
00:40:06,472 --> 00:40:07,669
What did He send you with.?

482
00:40:08,608 --> 00:40:14,989
He said: He sent me with a message of worshipping Him alone, associating no Gods with Him.

483
00:40:15,858 --> 00:40:18,979
and to destroy idols.

484
00:40:19,971 --> 00:40:22,169
He said: Can I follow you.

485
00:40:23,431 --> 00:40:29,341
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: You cannot follow me now; Don't you see my situation.

486
00:40:30,230 --> 00:40:36,092
But go back to your people and when you hear that I prevail then come and see me.

487
00:40:36,696 --> 00:40:39,581
Rasool Allah ﷺ knew that he will prevail one day.

488
00:40:39,896 --> 00:40:43,814
He said: When you hear that I have prevailed, come and meet me.

489
00:40:45,086 --> 00:40:55,043
So, Amr Bin Absaa(عمرو بن عبسه) said: I left and I would constantly ask about news, anything that relates to Muhammadﷺ.

490
00:40:55,493 --> 00:40:59,329
The travelers, I was always asked them, what is happening with Muhammadﷺ.

491
00:41:00,428 --> 00:41:08,671
Until one day I heard that Muhammadﷺ has migrated to Madina and he has been victorious.

492
00:41:08,938 --> 00:41:10,930
So, I went to meet him in Madina.

493
00:41:12,155 --> 00:41:15,889
He said; I approached Rasool Allah ﷺ and I asked him,

494
00:41:16,840 --> 00:41:17,799
"Do you know me?".

495
00:41:18,200 --> 00:41:27,042
This meeting now is years after he met with Rasool Allah ﷺ and he only met with Rasool Allah ﷺ for a very short time.

496
00:41:27,618 --> 00:41:30,510
So, he went into Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: Do you know who I am?

497
00:41:30,614 --> 00:41:32,056
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes.

498
00:41:32,231 --> 00:41:34,802
You are the man, who came and met me in Makkah.

499
00:41:35,307 --> 00:41:37,852
And see that's another leadership quality.

500
00:41:38,723 --> 00:41:40,084
You know your followers.

501
00:41:40,971 --> 00:41:43,962
You remember them you remember their names, you know about them.

502
00:41:44,714 --> 00:41:48,275
Sayyedina Sulaiman عليه السّلام was inspecting the army.

503
00:41:48,775 --> 00:41:54,228
And his army was composed of humans, Jin(جن), birds.

504
00:41:55,181 --> 00:42:03,256
So, it wasn't only restricted to one form of life, he had humans, Jin(جن), his Air Force was birds.

505
00:42:04,246 --> 00:42:07,875
And he noticed the absence of one soldier, Al-Hud-Hud(ألهدهد).

506
00:42:08,704 --> 00:42:10,294
One soldier was absent.

507
00:42:11,115 --> 00:42:14,810
And only Allah knows the number of his army, but he noticed his absence.

508
00:42:15,020 --> 00:42:16,699
Where is he.? He asked where's the Hud-Hud(هد هد).?

509
00:42:17,740 --> 00:42:23,033
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ remembered Amr Bin Absaa(عمرو بن عبسه), years after he met him.

510
00:42:23,151 --> 00:42:25,629
And he said: Yes, you are the man who came and met me Makkah.

511
00:42:26,111 --> 00:42:32,004
Amr Bin Absaa(عمرو بن عبسه) said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me of that knowledge which Allah has taught you,

512
00:42:32,610 --> 00:42:33,855
tell me about Salah( صلاة).

513
00:42:34,482 --> 00:42:37,267
Rasool Allah ﷺ described how to pray.

514
00:42:37,685 --> 00:42:42,823
And then he said, teach me about Wudhoo(وضؤ), and Rasool Allah ﷺ taught him Wudhoo(وضؤ).

515
00:42:43,861 --> 00:42:46,503
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

